<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  English strings.

  Two invariants are enforced by I18nResourceTest, and both are load-bearing:

  1. This file is key-for-key identical to values/strings.xml. A key added to one and not the
     other is a screen that silently falls back to Chinese on an English phone — which is how a
     half-translated app happens, one commit at a time.
  2. This file contains no CJK characters anywhere, comments included. That is why the section
     headings below are in English while the ones in values/strings.xml are not: a guard that has
     to exempt comments cannot tell a missed translation from a heading.

  Format specifiers must match the default file exactly (%1$s, %2$d, %3$s, and %% for a literal
  percent). The guard compares them per key, because a mismatch is not a cosmetic problem — it
  throws IllegalFormatException the moment the string is formatted.
-->
